						T Operating System

Wanted design

    self-hosted Operating System that can compile its own kernel,bootloader,etc in the os itself

To approach this

    * Create my own JIT x86 programming language escaping ELF shit hell  with also simple
      inline assembly syntax (not like GCC shit assebmly syntax)[named XXX].
    * Uses my own programming language to create all the kernel, bootloader, etc.
    * Create my own filesystem format [named idk yet].
    * Create XXXXXXX.c scripts to convert Linux directory of the source code of this to my own filesystem into the OS.
    * Create a Text editor in the OS so i can modify the OS source code inside the OS itself.
    * Create a compiler inside the OS so it can compile itself

    The approach is efficient because i don't need to Create the OS with GCC/ld ELF shit hell first.
    Which i can write my kernel on my own language even in the host OS (linux) and easily create the
    compiler in the OS too.

    So after you see the source on the github, its actually just the snapshot version of TOS ported to Linux
    github project.
